2026-09-06 v2.3.0 Inheritance is now optional; default = true. The previous
           always-on carry-over bled nested new options across all tiers
           because it could not tell an unset value from one left at its
           default - this opt-in version does not. With inheritance on, a
           scope inherits from the next higher tier only on the first use of
           that scope: a character inherits from Account on its first save of
           options, and Account inherits from Server level if Account is saved
           for the first time. With inheritance off, the first opening of a
           tier's saved vars loads your hard-coded defaults and no inheritance
           occurs. A one-time migration marks every already-populated scope as
           established, so existing installs keep their current per-tier values.

2026-09-03 v2.2.0 Added LEV.NewServerWideSavedVars - a truly server-wide,
           non-tiered saved-vars API (new ServerWideSavedVars.lua). Returns a
           proxy over one flat per-GetWorldName() store that ignores the
           Settings Scope dropdown / active-tier resolution entirely, for
           settings that must be one value for the whole megaserver regardless
           of which character/@account is logged in. Methods :GetRawTable(),
           :Version(), and :MigrateFrom() for a one-time lift of existing keys
           out of a tiered instance. Own load-guard flag
           serverWideSavedVarsVersion.

2026-08-05 v2.1.1 Fixed TieredSavedVars.lua's load-guard bug that made
           NewTieredSavedVars always error on first use, since the guard checked
           LibExtendedSavedVars.lua's version flag (already raised by the time
           TieredSavedVars.lua loads) instead of its own. Also reordered the LAM2
           scope dropdown to MegaServer, Account, Character to match the default
           scope.
